  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1247 PM CDT Mon Jul 27 2026\n\nLate on Tuesday, the ridge will slightly weaken dropping mid-level \nmoisture into the Texas Panhandle and northeastern New Mexico. A \nsurface pressure trough will extend from the central Texas Panhandle \ninto eastern New Mexico. Convection can be expected within this \nsurface trough but is expected to remain north and west of the \nregion. For the second half of the week, the upper ridge will \nmigrate westward and intensify over the southwestern US close to \n600dm or higher. Although a relief from the heat is unlikely, the \nmovement of the ridge may bring northwest flow convection beginning \non Thursday.",
